/-!
# A331016

Lexicographically earliest sequence of distinct positive terms that can be viewed as an irregular table where the n-th row has max(1, A001221(a(n))) terms and for n > 1, T(n, k) is a multiple of the k-th prime factor of a(n) (=A027748(a(n), k)).

The 67 terms known to OEIS, indexed from `1`.

Skeleton generated by `lake exe oeis-gen`; every declaration is a `sorry` placeholder.
-/

namespace A331016

/-- Known terms of `flat`, starting at index `1`. -/
def flatData : List flatRetType :=
  [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 9, 12, 8, 15,
    10, 18, 20, 14, 25, 16, 21, 22, 30, 24,
    7, 35, 26, 27, 28, 32, 11, 34, 33, 40,
